this is sandra sanchez for nexstar  media's border report  we're in la jolla texas and behind me is  about 50  families that were apprehended by border  patrol agents  this morning crossing the rio grande  they're a group here of about 25  unaccompanied  grandchildren um range from oldest  to seemingly youngest we have been told  we're not allowed to show their faces  so we're just shooting them from behind  one of the people behind me did speak to  me  said they've been waiting here a couple  hours they came to this country  because they want a better life  um  um  one little girl was cold and they were  giving her a blanket  and as border patrol waited for a bus  another group of migrants emerged from  the brush  they joined the existing group of  migrants to wait  for a bus  [Music]  so  a border patrol medic asked them how  they were feeling as an initial  screening for coronavirus  and as the sun began to rise they were  loaded onto buses  behind me there's a group of migrants  who are waiting to be transported by  border patrol  we've been out at the spot all morning  and we have seen about 200 people  apprehended by border patrol agents  some are unaccompanied minors they've  been loaded on buses  there was a horse patrol even that  helped to round up some of the people  who tried to run  run one border patrol agent told me but  most of the people are just  giving up they want to be apprehended  they're coming to the united states they  told me for a better life  [Music]  texas i'm sandra sanchez
 

